<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Serverless CI/CD with AWS SAM & GitHub Actions'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Serverless CI/CD with AWS SAM & GitHub Actions</h1>
  <p>Built a serverless application using AWS SAM and created a multi-stage CI/CD pipeline with GitHub Actions for automated Dev and Production deployments.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>AWS SAM</span><span>GitHub Actions</span><span>Lambda</span><span>API Gateway</span><span>CloudFormation</span><span>CI/CD</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/sam-pipeline.png" alt="AWS SAM Pipeline Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates building a <strong>serverless application</strong> using AWS SAM and automating deployments through a <strong>multi-stage CI/CD pipeline</strong> with GitHub Actions.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Initialized a serverless app using <strong>AWS SAM CLI</strong>.</li>
      <li>Built and tested Lambda locally using <strong>Docker</strong>.</li>
      <li>Bootstrapped pipeline resources for <strong>Dev and Prod</strong> stages.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>GitHub Actions</strong> for automated build, test, and deploy.</li>
      <li>Deployed infrastructure via <strong>CloudFormation</strong> stacks managed by SAM.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔄 CI/CD Flow</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — Source code & pipeline config</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub Actions</strong> — Build, test, deploy on push</li>
          <li><strong>S3 Artifact Buckets</strong> — Dev and Prod artifacts</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>⚡ Serverless Stack</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>AWS SAM</strong> — Packages & deploys via CloudFormation</li>
          <li><strong>Lambda Function</strong> — Python serverless app</li>
          <li><strong>API Gateway</strong> — REST API endpoint</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔐 Security</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>IAM Roles</strong> — Least-privilege per stage</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub Secrets</strong> — AWS credentials stored securely</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Pipeline Stages</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Push to main → <strong>GitHub Actions</strong> workflow triggered automatically.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>SAM builds and packages the application, uploads artifacts to <strong>S3</strong>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Deploys to <strong>Dev</strong> CloudFormation stack (sam-app-dev) and runs integration tests.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>On success, deploys to <strong>Production</strong> stack (sam-app-prod) with separate IAM roles.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Used <strong>sam init</strong> to scaffold a serverless app with best practices.</li>
      <li>Tested Lambda locally using <strong>sam local invoke</strong> with Docker.</li>
      <li>Bootstrapped multi-stage resources using <strong>sam pipeline init --bootstrap</strong>.</li>
      <li>Managed AWS credentials securely using <strong>GitHub Secrets</strong>.</li>
      <li>Understood how SAM abstracts CloudFormation for serverless deployments.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

